 "poem": "And, as a king mine vision,\nI have known the blood of all men's spirits\nIn many a night and day in heaven.\nThen say I was the second\nWhen her flesh gave forth the divine.\nWas it to my good or ill? We believe\nThat the pure with purebeasts are together,\nThat God's dear love set out to yourselves\nFrom one like you did from another.\nBut what is holy something\nYou will not know; 'tis more sweet than heaven,\nAnd sweeter still than earth below us.",
